The list uses the ruled 880px centered column (`width=880 align=center` on the tab-content). Rows follow the iOS AppRow anatomy — name headline, 2-line description, then NEUTRAL provider + status chips (server status string, capitalized; no invented Deployed/Building/Draft vocabulary), no leading icon, trailing chevron. The inline sort row and its accent-ring toggle are REMOVED (WP-N3, docs G4 precedent) — the sort dropdown lives in the anchored filter sheet (`modals/filter.surf`, Apps vocabulary: sort only), opened from the Sort button; the app count sits in the title row before the actions. The rows ⇄ grid switch is the `segmented-control` block — it NAVIGATES between the views (`?view=grid`, the c5 tasks mechanism reused); selection is server-stamped on the landing render, never faked. Sort is the only filter — Latest first / Name.

## Grid view

The grid view is the D-2 web addition: tinted apps-glyph tile (crossed hammer + wrench), single-line ellipsized name, 2-line clamped description, chips pinned to the card bottom, static uniform card heights, cards in a responsive multi-column grid inside the same ruled 880px column.

### Static grid markup (WP-C6 — the shape the live `?view=grid` route serves)

Grid mode is REAL block markup, not prose: each app authors as a row carrying the
leading tinted apps-glyph tile (`icon=apps`) — the anatomy difference from the
rows view, whose AppRow rows are icon-less. The multi-column card layout, the
2-line description clamp, and the bottom-pinned chips are chrome the renderer
does not emit for authored blocks yet (renderer-level gap, LOGGED for the 0.14.1
round); until then the cards stack as full-width tiled rows. Never the
source-driven site-page card blocks (`::features` / product grids are a
different lane). The rows ⇄ grid segmented-control NAVIGATES between the views
(`?view=grid`); selection is server-stamped, never faked.

